# Targets that chezmoi used to manage and must now be deleted on every machine.
#
# Removing a file from the source state only makes chezmoi stop managing it --
# the stale copy survives on workstations that already applied it. Listing the
# target here makes `chezmoi apply` actually delete it.
#
# Paths are relative to the destination dir (no leading ~/), globs are allowed,
# and directories are removed recursively. Entries are idempotent, so they stay
# here rather than being pruned once machines have caught up.

# Slash commands migrated to skills under dot_claude/skills (nothing remains
# under dot_claude/commands). Left in place, Claude Code still discovers these
# as commands and they shadow the skills that replaced them.
.claude/commands

